  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\sum_{r=1}^{13}\\left\\{\\frac{1}{\\sin \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}+(r-1) \\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right) \\sin \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}+\\frac{r \\pi}{6}\\right)}\\right\\}=a \\sqrt{3}+b, a, b \\in \\mathbf{Z}$, then $a^2+b^2$ is equal to :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$10$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$4$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$2$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$8$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\frac{1}{\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{6}} \\sum_{r=1}^{13} \\frac{\\sin \\left[\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}+\\frac{r \\pi}{6}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)-(r-1) \\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right]}{\\sin \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}+(r-1) \\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right) \\sin \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}+\\frac{r \\pi}{6}\\right)}$\n\n\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{1}{\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{6}} \\sum_{\\mathrm{r}=1}^{13}\\left(\\cot \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}+(\\mathrm{r}-1) \\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)-\\cot \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}+\\frac{\\mathrm{r} \\pi}{6}\\right)\\right) \\\\\n& =2 \\sqrt{3}-2=\\alpha \\sqrt{3}+\\mathrm{b}\n\\end{aligned}$\n\nSo $a^2+b^2=8$"
  }
}